# Line-ending policy — keep Windows checkouts from breaking the build.
#
# The load-bearing rule is *.patch: patches/bungee-stream-reset.patch is applied
# with `git apply` during the Bungee FetchContent step. If Git for Windows
# converts it to CRLF on checkout (the default core.autocrlf=true does this),
# the patch can fail to apply. Forcing LF here makes it machine-independent.
# (This file is already LF, so adding these rules causes no renormalization.)
#
# NOTE: .gitattributes only governs THIS repo. The Bungee/JUCE sources pulled by
# FetchContent are separate clones governed by the machine's global git config,
# so also run `git config --global core.autocrlf input` on the VM
# (see WINDOWS_VM_SETUP.md).

# Patches and build scripts must stay LF.
*.patch  text eol=lf
*.cmake  text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply end-of-line conversion (would corrupt them).
*.png    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.onnx   binary
*.data   binary
*.dll    binary
*.dylib  binary
*.component binary
*.vst3   binary
*.zip    binary
*.tgz    binary
